    "message": "feat(analytics): show when a fallback model answered\n\nFallback chains shipped in 4.31.0 with no way to tell they had fired. A\nrequest served by the second model in a chain looked identical to one served\nby a healthy primary: the row named the model that answered, which is correct,\nbut nothing said it was not the one the route picked. So a primary could be\nfailing every request, silently, and the dashboard would look fine.\n\nTwo new columns, both migrated with ALTER TABLE for existing databases:\nroute_attempt (0 for the route's own model, 1+ for a fallback) and\nroute_primary_model, recorded only when a later attempt answered because\notherwise it just repeats resolved_model.\n\nThe executor already called back on every attempt so analytics could name the\nmodel that answered; it now passes the attempt index with it, and the capture\nremembers the first model it saw.\n\nSurfaced three ways, because \"did failover happen\" and \"what is failing\" are\ndifferent questions:\n\n- a Served by fallback stat card, as count and share\n- a Failover panel listing primary -> what covered for it, by volume, so a\n  consistently failing primary is obvious\n- a badge on the affected table row, plus the full route in the detail panel\n\nRows written before this version have no route data at all, which is not the\nsame as \"no fallback was used\". The store counts non-null route_attempt\nseparately and the card renders an em dash rather than a reassuring 0% for\ntraffic it knows nothing about -- the same distinction the cache columns\nalready make, and for the same reason.\n\nVerified through the whole path with real data rather than per layer: drive\nRequestCapture the way the executor drives it (attempt 0, then attempt 1),\nfinish the capture, read the row back out of SQLite, then read the aggregate.\n\n    provider            cerebras\n    resolved_model      qwen-3\n    route_attempt       1\n    route_primary_model nvidia_nim/nemotron\n    served_by_fallback  1 of 1 reported\n    fallback_routes     [{'primary': 'nvidia_nim/nemotron',\n                          'served_by': 'cerebras/qwen-3', 'count': 1}]\n\n956 tests pass; ruff, ty and node --check clean; every new CSS class is\nemitted and every emitted class is styled.\n\nNot verified: no browser in this environment, so the badge and panel are not\nobserved rendering.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
